        "notes": [
          "1. Euler totient function of n1 with phi = (p - 1) × (q - 1), where p and q are prime factors of modulus n (see NIST SP800-56B Appendix C or RSA encryption/decryption principle for details). As optimization it is recommended to keep phi information as part of the key pair generation. Alternative is to store the key as (p, q, e, d) instead of (N, e, d, phi), in this case, to derive N and phi using PKA arithmetic multiplier: N=p×q, and phi = (p - 1) × (q - 1)."
